    <activity xml:id="activity-functions-real-life">

        <title>Exploring Functions Around Us</title>

        <p>
            Functions are used every day to describe relationships between quantities. The value of one quantity often depends on another quantity.
        </p>

        <p>
            Study the situations below and determine which quantity depends on the other.
        </p>

        <p>
            <ol marker="(a)">

                <li>
                    <p>
                        The total cost of buying mangoes depends on the number of kilograms purchased.
                    </p>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <p>
                        The distance travelled by a car depends on the time taken when moving at a constant speed.
                    </p>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <p>
                        The amount of money earned by an employee depends on the number of hours worked.
                    </p>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <p>
                        The temperature of a cup of tea changes with time as it cools.
                    </p>
                </li>

            </ol>
        </p>

        <p>
            Discuss the following questions.
        </p>

        <p>
            <ol marker="(i)">

                <li>
                    <p>
                        Which quantity is the input in each situation?
                    </p>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <p>
                        Which quantity is the output?
                    </p>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <p>
                        How can each situation be represented using a function rule?
                    </p>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <p>
                        Why are functions useful in describing real-life situations?
                    </p>
                </li>

            </ol>
        </p>

        <figure xml:id="fig-functions-real-life">
            <caption>Functions help describe relationships between quantities in daily life</caption>

            <image width="70%">
                <latex-image>
                    \begin{tikzpicture}[scale=1]

                        \draw[rounded corners, thick] (0,0) rectangle (3,1);
                        \node at (1.5,0.5) {Input};

                        \draw[-&gt;, thick] (3,0.5)--(5,0.5);

                        \draw[rounded corners, thick] (5,0) rectangle (8,1);
                        \node at (6.5,0.5) {Function Rule};

                        \draw[-&gt;, thick] (8,0.5)--(10,0.5);

                        \draw[rounded corners, thick] (10,0) rectangle (13,1);
                        \node at (11.5,0.5) {Output};

                    \end{tikzpicture}
                </latex-image>
            </image>
        </figure>

    </activity>


    <insight>

        <p>
            A function is a rule that connects one quantity to another quantity.
        </p>

        <p>
            In real life, functions are used whenever one value depends on another.
        </p>

        <p>
            Examples include
        </p>

        <p>
            <ul>

                <li>
                    <p>
                        The fare paid for a taxi ride depends on the distance travelled.
                    </p>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <p>
                        Electricity bills depend on the number of units consumed.
                    </p>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <p>
                        Mobile data usage depends on time spent online.
                    </p>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <p>
                        The area of a circle depends on the radius.
                    </p>
                </li>

            </ul>
        </p>

        <p>
            Functions help us predict values, solve problems, and make decisions in everyday life.
        </p>

        <p>
            A real-life function can be written using symbols.
        </p>

        <p>
            <me>C(x)=50x</me>
        </p>

        <p>
            This may represent the cost <m>C</m> of buying <m>x</m> exercise books at 50 shillings each.
        </p>

        <p>
            In this example
        </p>

        <p>
            <ul>

                <li>
                    <p>
                        <m>x</m> is the input or independent variable
                    </p>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <p>
                        <m>C(x)</m> is the output or dependent variable
                    </p>
                </li>

            </ul>
        </p>

    </insight>


    <example xml:id="ex-taxi-fare-function">

        <statement>
            <p>
                A taxi company charges a fixed fee of 200 shillings and an additional 50 shillings for every kilometre travelled.
            </p>

            <p>
                <ol marker="(a)">

                    <li>
                        <p>
                            Write a function to represent the total fare.
                        </p>
                    </li>

                    <li>
                        <p>
                            Find the fare for a journey of 8 kilometres.
                        </p>
                    </li>

                </ol>
            </p>
        </statement>

        <solution>

            <p>
                Let <m>x</m> represent the distance travelled in kilometres.
            </p>

            <p>
                The total fare consists of a fixed charge of 200 shillings together with 50 shillings for each kilometre travelled.
            </p>

            <p>
                The function is
            </p>

            <p>
                <me>F(x)=50x+200</me>
            </p>

            <p>
                Substitute <m>x=8</m> into the function.
            </p>

            <p>
                <md>
                    <mrow>F(8)\amp=50(8)+200</mrow>
                    <mrow>\amp=400+200</mrow>
                    <mrow>\amp=600</mrow>
                </md>
            </p>

            <p>
                The fare for the journey is 600 shillings.
            </p>

        </solution>

    </example>


    <example xml:id="ex-water-tank-function">

        <statement>
            <p>
                A water tank already contains 300 litres of water. Water flows into the tank at a rate of 25 litres per minute.
            </p>

            <p>
                <ol marker="(a)">

                    <li>
                        <p>
                            Write a function representing the amount of water in the tank after <m>t</m> minutes.
                        </p>
                    </li>

                    <li>
                        <p>
                            Determine the amount of water after 12 minutes.
                        </p>
                    </li>

                </ol>
            </p>
        </statement>

        <solution>

            <p>
                Let <m>W(t)</m> represent the amount of water after <m>t</m> minutes.
            </p>

            <p>
                The tank starts with 300 litres and gains 25 litres every minute.
            </p>

            <p>
                The function is therefore:
            </p>

            <p>
                <me>W(t)=300+25t</me>
            </p>

            <p>
                Substitute <m>t=12</m> into the function.
            </p>

            <p>
                <md>
                    <mrow>W(12)\amp=300+25(12)</mrow>
                    <mrow>\amp=300+300</mrow>
                    <mrow>\amp=600</mrow>
                </md>
            </p>

            <p>
                After 12 minutes, the tank contains 600 litres of water.
            </p>

        </solution>

    </example>


    <example xml:id="ex-mobile-data-function">

        <statement>
            <p>
                A mobile network charges 5 shillings per minute for a phone call.
            </p>

            <p>
                <ol marker="(a)">

                    <li>
                        <p>
                            Write a function representing the cost of a phone call lasting <m>m</m> minutes.
                        </p>
                    </li>

                    <li>
                        <p>
                            Find the cost of a 15-minute call.
                        </p>
                    </li>

                </ol>
            </p>
        </statement>

        <solution>

            <p>
                Let <m>C(m)</m> represent the total cost of the call.
            </p>

            <p>
                Since each minute costs 5 shillings:
            </p>

            <p>
                <me>C(m)=5m</me>
            </p>

            <p>
                For a 15-minute call:
            </p>

            <p>
                <md>
                    <mrow>C(15)\amp=5(15)</mrow>
                    <mrow>\amp=75</mrow>
                </md>
            </p>

            <p>
                The total cost of the call is 75 shillings.
            </p>

        </solution>

    </example>


    <exercises xml:id="ex-functions-real-life">

        <exercise>

            <statement>
                <p>
                    A shop sells pens at 40 shillings each.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <ol marker="(a)">

                        <li>
                            <p>
                                Write a function representing the total cost of buying <m>x</m> pens.
                            </p>
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            <p>
                                Find the cost of 12 pens.
                            </p>
                        </li>

                    </ol>
                </p>
            </statement>

            <answer>
                <p>
                    <ol marker="(a)">

                        <li>
                            <p><m>C(x)=40x</m></p>
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            <p><m>480</m></p>
                        </li>

                    </ol>
                </p>
            </answer>

        </exercise>


        <exercise>

            <statement>
                <p>
                    A farmer harvests 80 bags of maize each season and stores an additional 15 bags every week.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <ol marker="(a)">

                        <li>
                            <p>
                                Write a function representing the total number of bags after <m>w</m> weeks.
                            </p>
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            <p>
                                Determine the number of bags after 10 weeks.
                            </p>
                        </li>

                    </ol>
                </p>
            </statement>

            <answer>
                <p>
                    <ol marker="(a)">

                        <li>
                            <p><m>B(w)=80+15w</m></p>
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            <p><m>230</m></p>
                        </li>

                    </ol>
                </p>
            </answer>

        </exercise>


        <exercise>

            <statement>
                <p>
                    The perimeter of a square depends on the length of its side.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <ol marker="(a)">

                        <li>
                            <p>
                                Write a function for the perimeter of a square with side length <m>s</m>.
                            </p>
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            <p>
                                Find the perimeter when <m>s=9</m>.
                            </p>
                        </li>

                    </ol>
                </p>
            </statement>

            <answer>
                <p>
                    <ol marker="(a)">

                        <li>
                            <p><m>P(s)=4s</m></p>
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            <p><m>36</m></p>
                        </li>

                    </ol>
                </p>
            </answer>

        </exercise>


        <exercise>

            <statement>
                <p>
                    A savings account starts with 1,500 shillings and increases by 250 shillings every month.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <ol marker="(a)">

                        <li>
                            <p>
                                Write a function representing the amount saved after <m>m</m> months.
                            </p>
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            <p>
                                Find the amount saved after 6 months.
                            </p>
                        </li>

                    </ol>
                </p>
            </statement>

            <answer>
                <p>
                    <ol marker="(a)">

                        <li>
                            <p><m>S(m)=1500+250m</m></p>
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            <p><m>3000</m></p>
                        </li>

                    </ol>
                </p>
            </answer>

        </exercise>

    </exercises>

</section>
